  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What the context pays",
      "items": [
        "Without a proxy every server's catalog lands in the prompt before the first question; three servers of 40 tools is 120 definitions",
        "With mcprig the agent sees nine meta tools (five work with servers, four serve resources and prompts); list_commands brings a catalog on demand and caches it",
        "describe_commands sends one schema, invoke_many runs a batch in a single answer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What the operator gets",
      "items": [
        "One endpoint and one Bearer key per set, each set its own process and port — a crash of one leaves the others serving",
        "Panel: sets, servers, variables, keys with profiles, live calls, statistics with p50/p95, a ready-to-paste agent prompt",
        "Sandbox for stdio servers, OAuth for remote ones, import/export of the registry"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What it costs",
      "items": [
        "One more process per set and one indirection: a tool is reached as invoke_command{server, command_name}",
        "A schema the agent has not seen costs a describe_commands call, and list_commands returns the catalog in parts under maxBytes",
        "Single operator, one panel password, no per-user roles; CLI and log lines are Russian"
      ]
    }
  ]
}